### SOMS business-code segment regression script (VS Code REST Client)
### Business codes segmented by domain (see src/common/business-code.ts): 0 success / 10xxx general / 20xxx friend·invite / 30xxx message / 40xxx group / 50xxx federation / 60xxx push / 70xxx call
### Principle: business results always return HTTP 200 + code; only 401/404/409/500 keep HTTP codes for the system layer.
### Auth: a single opaque session token — browser uses the httpOnly cookie (no header); native uses Authorization: Bearer <sessionToken>. Fill data.sessionToken into @token below for the Bearer cases.

@host = http://localhost:3000/api/v1
@token =


### Swagger docs (open /api/v1/docs in a browser)
GET {{host}}/docs


### 1. register missing password → expect HTTP 200 / code 10000 (ValidationPipe folded into the business flow)
POST {{host}}/user/register
Content-Type: application/json

{"account": "test"}


### 2. register a new user → expect HTTP 200 / code 0
POST {{host}}/user/register
Content-Type: application/json

{"account": "demo_1234", "password": "123456"}


### 3. duplicate register → expect HTTP 200 / code 10002 (ALREADY_EXISTS)
POST {{host}}/user/register
Content-Type: application/json

{"account": "demo_1234", "password": "123456"}


### 4. login wrong password → expect HTTP 200 / code 10009 (INVALID_CREDENTIALS)
POST {{host}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{"account": "no_such_user", "password": "wrongpwd"}


### 5. access a protected route with no token → expect HTTP 401 / code 10003 (SessionAuthGuard, HTTP code retained)
POST {{host}}/user/my-profile


### 6. OTP login with a bad code → expect HTTP 200 / code 10012 (OTP_INVALID)
POST {{host}}/auth/otp/login
Content-Type: application/json

{"account": "demo_1234", "code": "000000"}


### Log in to get a session token (fill data.sessionToken from the response into @token above before running the cases below)
POST {{host}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{"account": "demo_1234", "password": "123456"}


### 7. resolve an unknown account → expect HTTP 200 / code 10001 (NOT_FOUND)
POST {{host}}/user/resolve
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"account": "no_such_user"}


### 8. invite yourself as a friend → expect HTTP 200 / code 20001 (FRIEND_SELF)
###    replace userId with your own id (get it from my-profile first)
POST {{host}}/invite/friend
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"userId": 10}
